# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — output routes to the session writer.
#
# Spec §9.1 / §14 exit-criterion 4: A's `echo "hi"` reaches A's output.
# We invoke __builtin_lobby_send directly via Lobby.__builtin_lobby_send;
# the direct call form continues to work and exercises the routing path
# independently of the Lobby.echo closure wrapper.  The v0.10.11 W4 fix
# makes Lobby.echo itself work (tested in tests/chk/lobby/lobby_echo_works.chk).
# This routes through __builtin_lobby_send →
# urbi_vm_write_in_realm → session writer → "kind":"output" envelope
# with the eval id.
#
# The cross-session non-routing aspect (A's output NOT reaching B/C/D)
# is verified by tests/unit/test_repl_multi_client.c (Task 33) over TCP.

> {"id":16,"op":"eval","code":"Lobby.__builtin_lobby_send(\"from-session\", \"\", \"***\")"}
< "id":16 | "kind":"output" | *** from-session
< "id":16 | "kind":"result"
< "id":16 | "kind":"done"
